vyos-1x-061-bonding-hw-offload.patch

LS1046A ASK2: `set interfaces bonding bondX offload ipv4|ipv6`. Adds the
offload leafs to the bonding interface definition; makes offload.ipv4/ipv6
inherited bond options so member re-commits keep the family mask the bond
owns (member apply arms the FMan port through the existing
EthernetIf.set_ask_offload() path); verifies the kernel contract (mode
802.3ad, MTU 1280..9000, members are FMan ports eth0-eth4; VPP mutex and
the existing member checks already apply); re-runs members + firewall on
offload leaf / member-set changes via the configd dependency machinery;
extends the patch 058 auto hardware flowtable to offloaded bonds (device =
bond master; ask.ko spreads ingress records across members itself) and
resolves flowtable devices to member ports for `ethtool -K
hw-tc-offload on` since the bond master owns no NETIF_F_HW_TC. Also fixes
interfaces_ethernet.py's bond-option inheritance copy to use
dict_set_nested(): dict_set() does not create intermediate keys, so
inheriting the multi-segment offload.ipv4/ipv6 leaves into a member without
an own "offload" node raised KeyError and failed the commit (upstream only
ever inherited the single-segment "mtu", which cannot trigger it).

Pairs with kernel Increments 1+2 (see doc/CHANGES-LACP.md upstream notes).

